    "specPath": "specs/010-integrations/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "A shared boundary contract for three independently optional integration crates: `rustev-aicortex` adapts attributed context and observation proposals, `rustev-rahi` adapts evidence delivery and optional operational hosting, and `rustev-serve` exposes bounded registered-plan execution over an application-operated service boundary. Every integration preserves explicit identity, provenance, failure and unresolved effects; none grants authority, owns domain judgment, or makes Rustev depend on an ecosystem service. Concrete external API bindings and readiness claims require later evidence before implementation.\n",
    "title": "Optional ecosystem integrations and serving boundary"
